  "note": "Nomination-day report for the electoral divisions of Cookstown rural district, one member each. Ten candidates were returned unopposed; no nominations were received for Beaghmore, Killeenan, Slatequarry, Pomeroy and Killycolpy. Stewartstown was the only contest, polled on Wednesday 28 May 1924. Sinclair (Official Unionist), 202; Burrows (Independent Unionist), 165; majority 37."
